cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CDFuse: a browser-based tool for comparing gridded NetCDF datasets"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Hrishikesh
    affiliation: "Department of Water Resources Development and Management, Indian Institute of Technology Roorkee"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hrishikesh618/CDFuse"
abstract: >-
  CDFuse compares two gridded NetCDF datasets. It aligns a candidate dataset
  against a reference dataset in time and space, calculates cell-wise
  performance metrics (Correlation, NSE, KGE, PBIAS, RMSE, MAE and Bias),
  renders maps, and exports reproducible outputs as PNG, NetCDF, GeoTIFF and
  CSV. The tool is dataset-neutral: no product-specific timestamp or
  accumulation conventions are assumed, and every such adjustment is left under
  explicit user control.
keywords:
  - netcdf
  - gridded data
  - model evaluation
  - validation metrics
  - xarray
  - hydrology
  - climate
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-06"
